From f3dc3ddd48de028e865141fe6ce20ba0f3a23179 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:10:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: blits into and out of 3D textures on the CPU

3D textures are linear and a resolve writes the tiled layout, so rendering
into them can't work, but st still blits into 3D resources (format
conversion on upload, readback through a 3D staging texture): the data
came out in 4-texel tile runs. Do 3D blits on the CPU with
util_format_unpack/pack_rgba and nearest scaling. The Xenos transfer path
also (de)tiles every layer of a box now, not only depth 1.
piglit texsubimage, texsubimage-unpack pass; texture-packed-formats 3D
drops from about 1100 failing probes to 216.

